@startuml uc006-design-sequence-startup-error
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-006 Run complete evaluation: design sequence (extensions 1a and 1c: the run cannot start)

actor Developer
participant "cli.main()" as Main
participant "cli.run_command()" as Run
participant "config.load_config()" as Config
participant "benchmark.load_benchmark()" as Bench
participant "judge.get_rubric()" as Rubric
participant "connector_factory" as Factory

Developer -> Main : judgelab run --config evaluation.yaml
opt 1c: --config is missing
  Main --> Developer : argparse prints usage, raises SystemExit(2)
end
Main -> Run : run_command(config_path, output_dir, connector_factory)
activate Run
note over Run
  Everything below is inside one try block.
  Each branch is reached only if the steps
  before it succeeded.
end note
alt config problem
  Run -> Config : load_config(config_path)
  Config --> Run : raises ConfigError("config file not found: ...", "... is not valid YAML\n(line 1, column 15)", "unknown section(s) extras", "unknown setting(s) modle",\n"must name an environment variable", ...); a ProfileError is re-raised as ConfigError
else dataset missing or invalid
  Run -> Bench : load_benchmark(config.dataset)
  Bench --> Run : raises BenchmarkError(path, problems)
else unknown rubric
  Run -> Rubric : get_rubric(config.rubric)
  Rubric --> Run : raises JudgeError("unknown rubric 'strict'; known: ...")
else connection cannot be created
  Run -> Factory : connector_factory(config.target)
  Factory --> Run : raises ConnectorAuthError("environment variable TARGET_KEY is not set"),\nor ProfileError(unknown provider, unsupported option)
end
Run -> Run : except (ConfigError, ProfileError, BenchmarkError,\nJudgeError, ConnectorError) as e
Run --> Developer : stderr: "error: {e}"
Run --> Main : 1
deactivate Run
Main --> Developer : exit code 1

note right of Run
  Business rule: setup problems are found before the first model call.
  evaluate(), utc_now() and write_report() are never reached:
  no model is called and no report is written (AC-006-06).
end note
@enduml
